WEBVTT

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:08.410
Being curled up in your blankets 
on the weekend is bliss.

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:13.340
I hope I have a nice dream.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.250
Sophie-chan, I just heard 
a loud bang! Are you okay?

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:29.590
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:31.750
You don't look fine!

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:08.480
<b>Episode 11</b>

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:08.480
<b>Cold Season</b>

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:15.690
I was just trying to put the figure 
I got today into my collection room.

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:18.550
But the room was so full 
that everything collapsed.

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:22.120
I didn't know you had so much stuff.

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:25.240
Sorry for scaring you in 
the middle of the night.

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:26.110
It's fine.

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:27.730
I'm just glad you weren't hurt.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:30.370
I'm totally fine, so go back to bed.

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:32.620
You sure you don't want 
me to help you clean up?

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:35.140
Yeah. I'll be fine.

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:36.600
Okay...

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.540
Goodnight, then.

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:41.840
Let's see...

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.720
Oh, an avalanche?

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:45.300
Don't step on anything.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.970
Yeah, yeah...

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:50.730
You always have so much stuff.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:56.360
Yes. Maybe it's time for a serious clean-up.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.400
I'll get rid of the things
 I don't need anymore.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:00.450
<b>Some Time Later</b>

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:04.990
"Indifference, not betrayal, 
is the greatest sin in love."

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:07.660
This manga's making me cry!

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:12.940
<i>That's so distracting.</i>

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:21.670
I wonder if Sophie-chan's done.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:25.890
<b>Don't Need</b>

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:25.890
Good morning, Akari.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:30.260
Have you been cleaning up this whole time?

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:33.340
Once I started, I couldn't stop.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:35.030
Really?

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:37.730
But because of that,

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:42.120
I've been able to get this shelf 
and this shelf perfectly clean.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:45.310
And I read all the manga on this shelf!

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:47.650
You didn't get anywhere!

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:53.000
All right!

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.370
I don't have school today, so I'll help, too.

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:57.210
Are you sure?

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.100
Yeah!

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:01.090
The other one came back 
so they could die together.

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:03.680
I'm crying...

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:10.640
<b>Hinata-chan</b>

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:12.890
<b>Need</b>

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:12.890
It's Hinata-chan.

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:17.860
<b>Tasty Potato Chips
</b>Lightly Salted

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:20.020
Akari, feel like going out somewhere?

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:22.390
I didn't really have anything 
particular in mind.

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:26.560
Sorry, but I'm helping 
Sophie-chan clean up today.

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:28.990
Sounds like a lot of work.
Want me to come help?

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:30.040
<i>You sure?</i>

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:31.280
Of course!

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:34.450
Heya!

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:36.200
Thanks for coming, Hinata-chan!

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:37.760
Sorry to have you come all this way.

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:38.870
It's fine.

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:41.090
Oh, Ellie's here, too.

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:42.590
Hello, Hinata.

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:45.790
If we've got Akari, Sophie,
 Ellie, and me here...

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:50.030
Cleaning a single room with 
four people should be a snap.

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:52.390
How reassuring.

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:56.940
There isn't even room for 
four people in here!

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:58.250
I'm glad to have you here.

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:02.010
Sophie-chan's been working 
hard since last night.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:04.160
There's no end in sight, though.

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:07.740
<b>Don't Need</b>

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:07.740
<b>Need</b>

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:06.450
I wonder why that is.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:11.480
So Ellie's not helping at all.
She's just reading manga.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.960
I agonize over every single item 
before I can throw it away.

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:18.750
Sophie...

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:25.680
<i>I guess she did say she's been storing 
books here that are over 100 years old.</i>

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:29.070
<i>I bet there are a lot of things 
that are significant to her.</i>

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:32.380
<i>I have to tread with caution.</i>

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:39.990
So this funny-shaped Styrofoam piece that 
was used as packing material in a package...

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:41.070
Throw it away already!

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.270
Okay!

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:51.440
It's starting to look better in here.

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:52.620
Yeah!

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:54.650
What's wrong?

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:57.570
I never finished reading this book.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:01.970
A Game Buoy! I haven't seen one in ages!

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:05.710
A Furbu doll! I used to have one of these!

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:07.260
Oh, look! It works!

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:11.150
If you enter a command on the 
boot-up screen, you can get items.

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:14.270
It still talks!

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:16.600
Oh, what a cute toy.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:18.230
<b>Many Minutes Later...</b>

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:22.240
It's so weird!

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:23.760
Funny, isn't it?

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:27.350
I used to play this game at my 
uncle's house when I was little.

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:29.690
Oh, there's a secret in that stage.

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:30.520
Cool!

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:32.440
Oh! The cleaning!

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:36.530
Oh, wow, it's a pager.

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:38.910
They're completely obsolete now.

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:40.630
What's that?

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:42.870
You haven't heard of these, huh?

00:06:43.690 --> 00:06:46.300
Back before cell phones were in common use,

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:49.710
people used these and 
communicated with numerical codes.

00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:54.940
I got one, but I didn't have 
anyone to communicate with.

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:57.200
Wow, I've never seen one before!

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:58.360
How cool!

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:01.690
I can't imagine a time without cell phones.

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:05.100
<i>I thought it was still 
relatively new technology.</i>

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:07.770
<i>High school girls today don't 
even know what this is?</i>

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:11.240
Well, you know, I'm but a 
fresh-faced youngster myself,

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:12.830
so I don't know much about them.

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:14.510
You're 360 years old.

00:07:14.510 --> 00:07:16.870
Why are you trying to hide that now?

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:21.440
This old newspaper's in English.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:24.490
Sophie, I can throw this away, right?

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:27.450
Old newspapers are useful when cleaning.

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:30.400
Oh, please save that one.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:33.930
There's an article about the Apollo 11
 in there that I want to keep.

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:36.030
Oh, that's famous!

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:37.130
There's a photo, too!

00:07:37.130 --> 00:07:38.500
That's amazing!

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:41.360
It's hard to imagine humans went 
to the moon decades ago.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:42.360
That looks like fun.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:43.820
What are you looking at?

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:50.820
Is that an ad for a sci-fi movie?

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:52.570
No, that actually happened.

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:57.250
My bookshelves are so full.

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:00.560
Maybe I should get rid of 
the ones I have as ebooks.

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:02.130
You've got so many books.

00:08:02.130 --> 00:08:04.590
I wonder if I've heard of any of them.

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:07.460
This book is well-known even now.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:08.830
I bet you've heard of it.

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:09.730
Huh?

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:12.490
It's <i>The Travels of Marco Polo</i>.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:17.060
It's been hundreds of years 
since I read it, though.

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:22.390
In it, Japan was spoken of
 as the Land of Gold.

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:24.600
It made me want to see this country someday.

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:29.940
Oh! So this book is the 
reason you came to Japan?

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:33.950
No, I actually came because 
I wanted to buy <i>Super Manio 2</i>.

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:35.620
You came here to buy a video game?!

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:41.160
What a cute ribbon!

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:44.390
Did you used to wear this kind of ribbon?

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:46.920
I'd love to see that!

00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:46.920
Uh, well...

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:51.630
Hey, that's the one I gave you 100 years ago.

00:08:53.030 --> 00:08:56.340
You seem to have kept it safe all this time.

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:59.060
You're so cute sometimes.

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:01.740
This is...

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:05.230
<b>The Year 191X</b>

00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:10.340
Well, Ellie gave these to me, 
but it's not the kind of thing I wear.

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:12.030
I'll return them to her.

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:16.740
<b>30 Years Later</b>

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:16.730
<i>A lot of time has passed, 
and I still haven't given them back...</i>

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:21.470
<i>We've never been out of touch this long.</i>

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:23.960
<i>I wonder if something happened to her...</i>

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:25.430
<b>Another 20 Years Later</b>

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:29.650
<i>I don't think Ellie is with us anymore.</i>

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:33.740
<i>Even if they're not my style,
I should keep these in Ellie's memory.</i>

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:43.130
Wow, so you've been holding
on to those for over 100 years.

00:09:43.130 --> 00:09:43.900
Yes.

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:46.110
I guess I don't need to do that anymore.

00:09:46.550 --> 00:09:47.510
I'll throw them out.

00:09:47.510 --> 00:09:49.810
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:52.550
All right.

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:54.530
We've got all the boxes in order.

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:56.490
And the magazines.

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:58.020
And I finished vacuuming.

00:09:58.020 --> 00:10:00.360
And I got through the very last volume.

00:10:05.030 --> 00:10:06.790
Looks like we're done cleaning.

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:08.290
It looks so tidy now!

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:11.190
It went fast since we all chipped in.

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:13.930
You just read manga the whole time.

00:10:13.930 --> 00:10:15.160
Did you say something, Hinata?

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:16.450
Nothing.

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:20.290
All this work has made me hungry, though.

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:21.510
You're right.

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:22.610
Me, too.

00:10:22.610 --> 00:10:24.190
Want to go to the convenience store?

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:25.020
No.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:29.650
You all helped me out today, 
so I'm going to treat you.

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:30.950
Really?

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:32.020
Awesome!

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:33.850
That's pretty nice of you.

00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:38.580
All right!

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:40.830
I'm going to try my hand at cooking.

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:42.500
<i>When she said she'd treat us...</i>

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:44.210
<i>She meant she was going to cook?</i>

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:49.280
<i>Can Sophie-chan even tell the 
difference between sugar and salt?</i>

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:53.680
Wow, I'm so looking forward 
to trying your cooking.

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:57.780
<b>Worry
Worry</b>

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:57.780
<b>Fret
Fret</b>

00:10:53.680 --> 00:10:57.310
Don't be afraid to ask if 
you have any questions.

00:10:57.310 --> 00:10:59.310
You know, let's just order in.

00:11:02.230 --> 00:11:03.960
That's so good!

00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:05.440
Yum!

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:08.610
I'm so sleepy.

00:11:08.610 --> 00:11:10.180
Yeah, it's already noon.

00:11:10.530 --> 00:11:14.140
Thanks, both of you.
You were a really big help.

00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:15.670
It's fine!

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:19.410
Maybe you can help me with 
rearranging my furniture next.

00:11:20.770 --> 00:11:23.490
Oh, that could be really helpful.

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:25.150
That would be easy.

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:27.120
You're welcome to call on me anytime.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:28.470
I will!

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:29.830
Me, too!

00:11:30.280 --> 00:11:34.500
<i>To think that I have this many friends 
who are willing lend me a hand.</i>

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:38.110
<i>Until recently, that was unimaginable.</i>

00:11:38.580 --> 00:11:41.100
I'm so full.

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:43.080
Thanks for the food!

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:48.670
I'm going to keep this box as 
a memento of this fateful day.

00:11:48.670 --> 00:11:52.020
We just cleaned up! Don't start 
hoarding useless junk right away!

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:54.980
<b>A Few Days Later...</b>

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:57.190
Thank you very much.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:57.190
<b>Shokugan • Capsules
Figures
Comics • Videos</b>

00:11:57.190 --> 00:12:01.750
<i>I guess selling all that stuff 
I didn't need really added up.</i>

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:09.250
<i>I need to be careful so that room 
won't get cluttered up again right away.</i>

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:11.720
<i>I'd better avoid unplanned purchases.</i>

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:23.670
<i>It's a realistic figure from 
a legendary anime show!</i>

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:26.970
<i>If I got it now, I'd actually have room for it.</i>

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:31.320
<i>But I only just got my friends 
to help me clean up.</i>

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:38.690
<i>After about an hour of struggling, 
I still couldn't decide.</i>

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:41.410
How do you do?

00:12:41.410 --> 00:12:42.980
I came over to hang out!

00:12:42.980 --> 00:12:44.840
Hmm, I see.

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:48.590
You look a bit down.

00:12:48.590 --> 00:12:50.160
Did something happen?

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:55.040
It's just that Akari seems 
kind of strange today.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:58.390
Isn't Akari always kind of strange, though?

00:12:58.390 --> 00:13:04.010
Sure, but her face seems flushed, 
and her breathing is labored.

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:05.260
<b>Pant</b>

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:05.880
<b>Pant</b>

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:06.510
<b>Pant</b>

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:07.260
<b>Pant</b>

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:08.260
<b>Pant</b>

00:13:07.480 --> 00:13:11.820
Let's play dress-up, Sophie-chan!

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:08.760
<b>Pant</b>

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:09.260
<b>Pant</b>

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:10.010
<b>Pant</b>

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:10.760
<b>Pant</b>

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:11.770
<b>Pant</b>

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:12.310
<b>Pant</b>

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:14.900
That's completely normal for her.

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:17.730
Maybe you're right.

00:13:28.090 --> 00:13:30.900
Looks like I caught a cold.

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:32.510
So you're sick?!

00:13:32.510 --> 00:13:33.080
Oh, my.

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:35.040
What do we do at a time like this?

00:13:36.020 --> 00:13:38.240
I have a little bit of 
medical knowledge, you know.

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:39.780
Let me take care of this.

00:13:39.780 --> 00:13:41.500
You do? That's great!

00:13:42.930 --> 00:13:46.190
The symptoms are... a runny nose.

00:13:46.190 --> 00:13:47.370
Anything else?

00:13:47.770 --> 00:13:50.840
Well... I feel cold.

00:13:51.460 --> 00:13:54.990
It looks like, of the four humors, 
you have too much phlegm.

00:13:55.610 --> 00:13:57.560
The four humors?

00:13:58.470 --> 00:14:01.050
You need to increase your 
yellow bile to balance it.

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:02.830
Yellow bile?

00:14:02.830 --> 00:14:04.900
From what century is 
this medical knowledge?

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:13.900
Yellow bile is associated 
with the fire element,

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:16.280
so warming up your body is important.

00:14:16.280 --> 00:14:18.450
I don't really get what you're talking about,

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:20.700
but making her warmer 
seems to be good for her.

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:24.240
Yeah, I do feel better now.

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:27.420
Then how about some bloodletting?

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:27.470
<b>Blood</b>

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:31.050
<b>Letting</b>

00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:31.050
That's just you wanting to see blood.

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:39.110
<i>Looks like Ellie's knowledge 
isn't that reliable.</i>

00:14:39.530 --> 00:14:43.240
Akari, do you know how to cure colds?

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:44.950
Um...

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:45.970
Yes?

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:50.480
I feel like licking you might cure it...

00:14:51.810 --> 00:14:52.930
This is bad.

00:14:52.930 --> 00:14:56.450
The cold is preventing her from 
having coherent thoughts.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:58.110
The <i>cold</i> is?

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:03.720
I'm going to call and ask what I should do.

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:05.100
Who are you calling?

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:08.050
What's up, Sophie? You don't normally call.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:10.460
<i>Hinata, I wanted to ask you something.</i>

00:15:10.460 --> 00:15:11.980
Okay, shoot.

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:15.640
Well, Akari has a cold, and I was—

00:15:15.020 --> 00:15:16.850
<i>Akari has a cold?!</i>

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:18.150
Hinata, are you there?

00:15:18.150 --> 00:15:19.270
Hello?

00:15:19.670 --> 00:15:21.320
The line cut out.

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:22.850
Try calling her back.

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:25.810
I keep calling, but she doesn't pick up.

00:15:25.810 --> 00:15:27.000
What's going on?

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:28.190
That's so weird.

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:30.750
Akari, are you okay?!

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:31.760
Oh, my.

00:15:32.180 --> 00:15:33.570
<i>She rushed over here.</i>

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:36.770
Her fever is kinda high.

00:15:36.770 --> 00:15:39.160
So should I call an ambulance?

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:41.800
That's going a bit far.

00:15:42.230 --> 00:15:44.240
She's right.

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:46.960
So we don't have to take her to 
the hospital and check her in?

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:50.720
I don't need a hospital.

00:15:52.270 --> 00:15:55.060
Does she mean she's beyond help?

00:15:55.060 --> 00:15:57.230
Is there nothing we can do to save her?

00:15:57.230 --> 00:15:58.390
Calm down.

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:00.920
It's not that serious.

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:03.990
It's okay.

00:16:03.990 --> 00:16:06.820
This isn't like back when the 
black death was going around.

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:11.280
She just dropped that horrifying 
term like it's no big deal.

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:14.880
Just make sure she doesn't get too cold,

00:16:14.880 --> 00:16:17.540
keep her well-nourished and rested, 
and she'll be better in no time.

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:18.720
I see.

00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:21.320
Akari, I'm going to peel 
you an apple now, okay?

00:16:21.320 --> 00:16:22.990
I brought it from my house.

00:16:22.990 --> 00:16:24.250
Yay!

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:27.850
Ouch!

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:31.450
Ow!

00:16:32.020 --> 00:16:35.680
Wait, are you making us food, too?

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:36.850
No!

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:42.520
Thank you!

00:16:43.070 --> 00:16:46.930
I don't want all of you 
to catch it too, though.

00:16:46.930 --> 00:16:50.410
We're not like humans,
so don't worry about us.

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:51.280
Yeah.

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:54.350
<i>If I did catch a cold, though...</i>

00:16:56.230 --> 00:16:57.970
Open wide!

00:16:57.970 --> 00:16:59.170
Ahh...

00:16:59.730 --> 00:17:02.150
I don't mind catching it at all!

00:17:02.150 --> 00:17:03.740
No!

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:05.980
I'm sure you won't get sick, Hinata.

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:10.390
That reminds me. I was doing 
chores when this started.

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:11.970
I'll go finish that real quick.

00:17:11.970 --> 00:17:13.920
I'll finish it. You get some rest.

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:15.430
That's right.

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:17.680
Is there anything else we can do?

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:19.350
Well...

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:23.230
Can I ask you to take 
care of my dolls for me?

00:17:23.920 --> 00:17:27.890
They'll be fine if you leave them 
alone for a few days, won't they?

00:17:28.320 --> 00:17:31.430
But some of them get angry if 
you stop taking care of them.

00:17:32.020 --> 00:17:34.480
Don't just drop horrifying 
statements like that.

00:17:37.070 --> 00:17:39.680
I'm getting so hot.

00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:41.580
Did your fever get worse?

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:44.810
You're really hot.

00:17:46.050 --> 00:17:50.410
Your hand is so nice and cool.

00:17:50.410 --> 00:17:51.510
Really?

00:17:51.510 --> 00:17:54.390
Can you just stay like this for a while?

00:17:54.390 --> 00:17:55.370
My, my...

00:17:55.370 --> 00:17:58.580
Hmm... I don't mind doing it for a while,

00:17:58.580 --> 00:18:01.230
but cold things aren't 
good for you right now.

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:02.630
Wait!

00:18:09.850 --> 00:18:11.930
You're so cool.

00:18:10.910 --> 00:18:13.950
Hey! You're not supposed to get cold!

00:18:13.950 --> 00:18:15.300
Are you trying to kill yourself?

00:18:15.300 --> 00:18:18.430
When you have a high fever, 
cooling down is good.

00:18:18.430 --> 00:18:19.530
That's right!

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:22.640
I bet this will fix me right up!

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:20.950
<b>Squeeze</b>

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:22.700
<b>Lovey</b>

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:23.450
<b>Dovey</b>

00:18:22.640 --> 00:18:24.960
<i>Sophie's so lucky.</i>

00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:28.200
I see... So that's how it works.

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:37.030
Akari, are you cured now?

00:18:37.030 --> 00:18:40.210
I-It's not going to go away that quickly.

00:18:40.210 --> 00:18:44.180
Well, my body temperature 
is the same as Sophie's.

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:48.530
Thank you, Ellie-chan.

00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:50.690
That's the perfect amount of coolness.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:51.810
Really?

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:54.030
Then let me scoot closer.

00:18:55.270 --> 00:18:58.040
I'm going to lower my body 
temperature with ice water.

00:18:58.040 --> 00:18:58.990
I'll go use your bath.

00:18:58.990 --> 00:19:01.680
No! You'll catch a cold, too!

00:19:08.650 --> 00:19:10.410
It looks like she fell asleep.

00:19:10.410 --> 00:19:11.850
Yeah.

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:16.290
It looks like she's doing better now,
so I'll be heading home.

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:17.570
Take care getting back.

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:21.500
If you have any questions, 
just give me a call anytime.

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:22.410
Okay.

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:23.860
You really helped us out.

00:19:25.130 --> 00:19:27.480
We should get something to eat, too...

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:33.900
Sophie-chan... always...

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:40.230
Oh, my... Looks like I'm the third wheel.

00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:47.600
I slept so well!

00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:49.790
I think my fever went down.

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:51.580
I feel a lot better.

00:19:59.150 --> 00:20:01.300
Sophie-chan...

00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:04.040
You were by my side this entire time.

00:20:07.050 --> 00:20:08.660
Good morning, Sophie-chan.

00:20:08.660 --> 00:20:10.840
Akari, you're awake.

00:20:10.840 --> 00:20:13.530
How are you feeling? Any better?

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:19.540
<i>I am feeling better, but I wouldn't mind 
being taken care of a little longer.</i>

00:20:21.370 --> 00:20:23.610
Actually, still not so good.

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:26.780
<b>Crushed...</b>

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:28.900
So you <i>are</i> going to die after all?

00:20:28.900 --> 00:20:31.790
No, I lied! I'm a lot better now!

00:20:32.240 --> 00:20:35.210
<i>She's such a sweet vampire.</i>

00:21:41.320 --> 00:21:47.030
<b>Episode 12</b>

00:21:41.320 --> 00:21:47.030
<b>The Vampire and the Changing Seasons</b>

00:22:08.970 --> 00:22:11.170
That was great!

00:22:11.690 --> 00:22:14.890
Hey, Sophie, do you have more 
volumes of this manga?

00:22:11.690 --> 00:22:14.890
<b>Museum in Another World</b>

00:22:16.100 --> 00:22:18.340
I think they're in Akari's room.

00:22:23.450 --> 00:22:26.010
Humans sleep at this hour, so let's be quiet.

00:22:26.010 --> 00:22:27.770
I know that.

00:22:31.690 --> 00:22:34.900
Sneaking into a maiden's room at night

00:22:34.900 --> 00:22:37.690
is pretty appropriate for a vampire,
if you ask me.

00:22:37.690 --> 00:22:39.870
Hey, keep it down!

00:22:39.870 --> 00:22:43.120
Okay, you got the manga you were looking for,

00:22:43.120 --> 00:22:45.590
so let's leave quietly before she wakes up.

00:22:47.260 --> 00:22:51.740
Sophie-chan, let's play dress-up!

00:22:52.230 --> 00:22:53.670
Hey, Sophie...

00:22:54.130 --> 00:22:55.010
What is it?

00:22:55.390 --> 00:22:57.640
Humans sure are sad, huh?

00:22:57.640 --> 00:23:00.730
They have to sleep in this thing 
with no walls and no cover.

00:23:02.400 --> 00:23:04.190
Now that you mention it, you're right.

00:23:08.600 --> 00:23:11.180
Let's at least put a lid over her.

00:23:11.590 --> 00:23:14.670
I found a perfect styrene 
board in the storage room.

00:23:14.670 --> 00:23:15.980
Great idea!

00:23:17.210 --> 00:23:18.990
There we go. Perfect.

00:23:18.990 --> 00:23:21.760
She should sleep a bit better now.

00:23:21.760 --> 00:23:22.830
You're right.

00:23:23.440 --> 00:23:25.020
We did a good thing.

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:34.850
Sophie-chan, this room's ceiling 
is falling down on me.

00:23:34.850 --> 00:23:38.370
<i>That night, I was plagued by nightmares.</i>
